# Website rebuild rules

When working under `apps/web` (or creating it):

- Follow the **ryr-website** skill (same process as the mobile Nest rebuild).
- **Legacy UI first (mandatory):** Before building or restyling any screen, check `RentYourRideLegacy/Web-old` (`src/screens`, related SCSS/components). If that screen already exists, **match its layout, copy, colors, fonts, and assets** — do not invent a new design. Wire data to Nest `/v1` APIs (not the legacy backend).
- Dev/default API: `https://bedev.rentyourride.ca`. Production builds must use `https://backend.rentyourride.ca`.
- Production Stripe must be `pk_live_…`; never ship bedev + live Stripe (or prod API + `pk_test_…`) by accident.
- Do not fold admin dashboard work into the customer site (`apps/admin` is separate).
- Prefer TypeScript + a modern React toolchain (Vite or Next). Do not continue the legacy CRA app as the long-term codebase.
